# Release go/no-go: the runner's run over the public testbed's `core`, at the commits the release will tag. Fill each
# ref with a full 40-hex commit SHA, then copy this file to tests/integration/.env.local before the run. The runner
# clones the components and the testbed itself and configures `core` as the CI testbed stage does
# (tests/testbed/run-testbed-stage.sh). Relative paths resolve against the living-doc checkout (see
# docs/_integration/README.md § Release go/no-go).
TARGET=testbed
# The testbed's `master`, as a full commit SHA: git ls-remote https://github.com/AbsaOSS/living-doc-testbed master
TESTBED_REF=36a0ee65ad11df7588cd74a505ea1ace1ef7abc9
# The living-doc-collector-gh candidate: the full SHA of its `master` once its release pin pull request merged. An
# empty ref runs the pin in tests/collector/collector-pins.env, which is no candidate.
COLLECTOR_GH_REF=b197a608d2dfc816a2934ae4fa6f2cdf3fb5b611
# The living-doc-toolkit candidate: the full SHA of its `master` once its release pin pull request merged.
TOOLKIT_REF=fea9aa62d7805fbc675a5816f513a7d0259b7075
# The living-doc-generator-markdown candidate: the full SHA of its `master` once its release pin pull request merged.
GENERATOR_MARKDOWN_REF=005a058ae6b248a66c34e8bacdbe2217bb2a981d
OUT_DIR=docs/_integration/go-no-go/testbed-core
# Empty tries python3, then python. On Git Bash for Windows, python3 may be the Microsoft Store alias: set
# PYTHON=python.
PYTHON=
